      "lang": "en",
      "relatedTarget": "http://127.0.0.1:18770/leetcode/214/#step1",
      "excerpt": "02Turn a palindrome into equal endsHow can equal pieces identify the longest palindromic prefix? Let t = s + # + reverse(s), where # is a separator absent from the input. A border is a prefix that is also a suffix and is shorter than the whole string. We record its length.abac#cabaaba = aba → ℓ = 3Keep abac: t = abac#caba. Its first aba equals its last aba, so ℓ=3; length 4 fails because abac ≠ ca"
    }
